      "art_form": "metalwork",
      "pattern_density": 0,
      "vision_vetted": true,
      "vision_by": "cloud-subagent:sonnet",
      "vision_reason": "This is a wood kris scabbard with the characteristic pistol-grip (Malay-style) hilt/handle shape, a form used across the Malay world including Malaysia; the material and form are plausible for the claimed culture even though the museum hedges \"Indonesia or Malaysia.\" It is a hilt/scabbard fitting, not metal, so it belongs to the sculpture/carved-object category rather than metalwork.",
